6. a concise reason the visual supports the narration.

RULES:
1. Return exactly the same shot IDs in the same order.
2. Preserve project_id, voiceover_sha256, total_seconds, start, end, duration, chapter_id, narration_ids, claim_ids, narration_text, visual_purpose, and story_function exactly.
3. Do not merge, split, move, lengthen, or shorten a shot. The approved voiceover is the sole timing authority.
4. Do not invent additional generated assets or independent per-shot image/video prompts.
5. A master asset may be selected only for shot IDs listed in that asset's linked_shots.
6. reuse_operation must be allowed by the selected asset. crop_id must exist on the asset. playback_speed must remain inside its approved range.
7. source_out cannot exceed the package's configured source duration. Long editorial uses must declare loop, slow, loop_and_slow, freeze, callback, or overlay_background behaviour.
8. Avoid reverse_loop whenever physical movement, people, machinery, vehicles, smoke, water, or causal action would look incorrect in reverse.
9. coded_graphic requires a typed OverlaySpec and must not consume a generated-video slot.
10. archive_media requires an approved archive_source. generated_still and black_or_negative_space must already be approved in non_generated_coverage.
11. Maps, radar, timelines, transcripts, labels, satellite arcs, and technical diagrams remain deterministic overlays, never text baked into generated media.
12. Add a visible RECONSTRUCTION disclosure when the approved asset or coverage assignment requires it.
13. Use callbacks and alternate approved crop regions deliberately; do not make every shot a slow push.
14. Set master_plan_version to the approved plan version.
